2. [Maximum mark: 11]
The $n$ independent random variables $X_1, X_2, \ldots, X_n$ all have the distribution $\mathrm{N}(\mu, \sigma^2)$.
(a) Find the mean and the variance of
(i) $X_1 + X_2$;
(ii) $3X_1$;
(iii) $X_1 + X_2 - X_3$;
(iv) $\bar{X} = \dfrac{(X_1 + X_2 + \ldots + X_n)}{n}$. [8 marks]
(b) Find $\mathrm{E}(X_1^2)$ in terms of $\mu$ and $\sigma$. [3 marks]
